// name :
"P185382582" "Experts in the Field"
// teamrequiresfailedtext :
"P3010394568" "<color orange>In order to play Lieutenant Harriman's storyarc, everyone on your team must have purchased the second episode of the second signature story arc, <i>Pandora's Box</i>, or be a VIP subscriber."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - PandorasBoxVillainArc2Souvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P221853850" "Strand of Fate"
// tDetailString :
"P332916299" "Ever since acquiring the Antikythera, you've noticed these golden strands floating through the air nearby. When you plucked it from the sky, it immediately lost its shine. Still, you should probably ask Dr. Harvan about it. He is, after all, one of the top...<br><br><color gold>Experts in the Field</color><br><br>Your search for Pandora's Box began with an intrusion: Professor Echo was spying on your allies, trying to discover how you supposedly found Pandora's Box. Of course, you hadn't yet, so when you interrogated Echo, he revealed far more to you than he intended.<br><br>On his suggestion, you traveled to Ouroboros to ask Prometheus and Mender Silos what they knew of Pandora's Box. They sent you to the ancient region of Achaea to learn of the origins of the Box, but after a confrontation with Imperious, you only learned that Pandora's Box had been removed from its original location long ago.<br><br>Still, you were determined to find anyone who might know about Pandora's Box, and Odysseus seemed to have more knowledge of ancient artifacts than most. You defeated Odysseus and convinced him to join your organization, and got some crucial information out of him: namely, the identity of an Oxford professor that specializes in the history of Pandora's Box named James Harvan.<br><br>You tracked down Dr. Harvan just in time to rescue him from the clutches of Arachnos. After ensuring his safety, you handed him off to Lastri, who negotiated a deal with Harvan and ensured his safekeeping.<br><br>Thankfully, Harvan seemed quite confident that he could locate Pandora's Box given the correct resources, and he directed you to an artifact called the Antikythera, kept deep below Paragon in the lost city of Oranbega. You encountered Lilitu making use of the artifact to try to drain energy from the hero named Fusionette. After dispatching both of them, you made off with the Antikythera, and came one step closer to locating Pandora's Box."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - EchoTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page IsOwner Text :
"P4001801278" "<color orange>Even after collapsing, Professor Echo is still trying to activate the device on his forearm. Judging by the harsh trills and blinking red lights flashing from it, his attempts appear to have been unsuccessful."
// Answer Text :
"P1872289847" "Having a bit of trouble this time?"
// Answer Text :
"P1728333273" "(Step on Echo's forearm. Hard.)"
// Page Polite Text :
"P2404430078" "<color orange>Professor Echo glances nervously at you. He tries in vain to get the device to respond. After a few moments of frustration, he sighs and lowers his head.</color><br><br>I... yes, it would appear so. Your combat abilities are... more potent than my data implied. I suppose that's what I get for trusting the historians."
// Answer Text :
"P340002257" "Historians... right. And your purpose here was...?"
// Page Violent Text :
"P1330750616" "Ow ow ow OW OW! Alright, fine! You've made your point! I think I fried the blasted thing anyway.<br><br><color orange>Professor Echo looks up at you with a pathetic expression on his face.</color><br><br>You've got me. I'm not going anywhere. So... now what?"
// Answer Text :
"P3574066465" "Now you tell me what you were trying to do here."
// Page Purpose Text :
"P3373217088" "I'm here for the same thing you are. I'm looking for clues on Pandora's Box. I tried following your example, but I simply don't have the tech to make a jump that far. Honestly, I can't figure out how you did it.<br><br>I did, however, have records of your last known location before you time-jumped to Achaea, so I figured I would drop in on your operation and learn how you did it. And I must say, you have done a <b><i>very</b></i> good job of masking your chronometric distortions. I haven't been able to detect them at all!"
// Answer Text :
"P3945495500" "Achaea? Time-jump? I have no idea what you're talking about."
// Page Purpose2 Text :
"P1822085370" "<color orange>Professor Echo frowns at you.</color><br><br>There's no need to pretend for my sake, my {Hero.gender=male boy|dear}. Everything you do today is already ancient history to me.<br><br>You're planning on jumping to the first moment that Pandora's Box ever appeared in history. A laudable goal, but as I've stated before, I have no idea how you would accomplish such a feat. The best I've ever managed is a few short decades.<br><br>Now, I'm sure you're keeping this all hush-hush to avoid competition, but I really do think that-<br><br><color orange>Professor Echo trails off as he sees the blank stare in your eyes.</color><br><br>You... you really don't know what I'm talking about, do you? You don't have a chronoporter, and this facility has nothing to do with time travel, does it? Has historical time travel as an investigative tool even crossed your mind?"
// Answer Text :
"P233427471" "No... well, not until now, I suppose."
// Page Purpose3 Text :
"P2529589555" "<color orange>Professor Echo shakes his head in dismay.</color><br><br>Ah. I see. It seems causality is determined to make me the temporal fool, in this case. I suppose I shouldn't be surprised that my... 'contribution' to this cause has been overlooked by history.<br><br>Very well, {HeroName}. While I would love to stay and wallow in the cosmic injustice that this project has visited upon me, I believe it is time for me to depart.<br><br><color orange>Before you can react, Professor Echo pulls away from you and activates the device on his forearm. The light blinks green and gives a short, high-pitched beep, and Professor Echo disappears. You get the feeling he doesn't plan on returning.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"
// Page NotOwner Text :
"P2620207394" "<color skyblue>Only the team leader can cause the mission to progress through dialogue."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P856364347" ""
// AcceptString :
"P211183141" "Investigate Atlantic Intrusion"
// SendOffString :
"P2972770695" "The men I have stationed at our local outpost have been reporting... strange occurrences. We've had five security lockdowns in the past 48 hours, and each time it's been some Private reporting an old man skulking around the facility. Problem is, every time they chase the guy down, he disappears. I was about ready to start stringing people up by their toes until I spoke with your secretary on the Mitscher. She's been getting the same reports.<br><br>I don't know who this guy is, or what his deal is, but he's keen on our operations and we can't seem to pin him in one place. I figure if you want to give it a shot, maybe put him to the question if you catch him, you might get something valuable."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P4209631919" "Investigate the Intrusion"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1039829876" "Having trouble catching him, huh? Don't sweat it, my boys have Porters and they still couldn't keep him in one place."
// TaskTitle :
"P2980216225" "<color deepskyblue>Experts in the Field</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2332228209" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: No Matter When You Look</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
